{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. ___. I'm Dr. ___, one of your hospitalists. You've just come back from your bronchoscopy, and I wanted to check in on how you're feeling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’m okay, still a bit groggy. My chest feels sore, especially near the trach site. But I can breathe fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. The procedure involved dilating some narrowed areas in your airway, so some discomfort is expected. The team noted mild stenosis just below your trach, and the left main stem was quite tight — they opened it up to 9mm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the bronchus intermedius? Was that narrowed again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it was narrowed. They dilated it to 4mm. No complications during the procedure. Your oxygen levels stayed stable, and your chest X-ray afterward was clear — no pneumothorax or fluid."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. The pain is manageable, but oxycodone usually works better than Tylenol for me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Noted. We’ll keep you on oxycodone 5mg every six hours as needed. You’re on 40% trach mask now, and your saturations are 98%, which is excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I took all my morning meds today — prednisone, losartan, the Esbriet, and the inhaled tobramycin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. We’ll continue all your home medications. The Esbriet dose is being gradually increased, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’m on the third step — three capsules three times a day now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. That’s for the lung fibrosis related to your ___ syndrome. We’re also continuing your prednisone for the relapsing polychondritis. You’re on 7.5mg daily, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. I know I’ve been on it a long time. I’m careful about not missing doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s important. Because you’re on chronic steroids, your body may not respond well during an illness. If you get sick — fever, nausea, vomiting — you’ll need to triple your dose for three days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that from last time. What if I can’t take the pill?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re sending you home with a Solu-Cortef injection — 100mg. If you’re unconscious, severely ill, or can’t swallow, someone can give you that shot and you must go to the ER immediately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that’s reassuring. Should I get a MedicAlert bracelet?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2138-04-19 11:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we strongly recommend it. It could save your life in an emergency."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2138-04-19 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’m back to check on your pain. How’s it been since your last dose?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2138-04-19 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. The oxycodone helped. Still a dull ache, but no sharp pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2138-04-19 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. We’ll keep monitoring. Your labs came back — white count is a bit high at 18.6, but that’s likely from inflammation or your chronic condition, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2138-04-19 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from the polychondritis or the pseudomonas?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2138-04-19 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely the inflammation. You’re colonized with pseudomonas, so we’re continuing inhaled tobramycin, but there’s no sign of active infection this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2138-04-19 12:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my GERD? I’ve been using famotidine daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2138-04-19 12:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’re keeping you on famotidine. Controlling acid reflux helps protect your airway, especially with your trach and history of narrowing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2138-04-19 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just reviewing your chest X-ray from this morning — it shows some bibasilar atelectasis, meaning the lower parts of your lungs are a bit collapsed. But no pneumonia or pneumothorax."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2138-04-19 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I be doing more with the incentive spirometer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2138-04-19 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Keep using it every hour while awake. Deep breaths help re-expand those areas. The physical therapist will stop by later to assist."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2138-04-19 16:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "How’s your voice? I notice you’re whispering."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2138-04-19 16:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Still hoarse. I haven’t had a real voice since the trach. But I can communicate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2138-04-19 16:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Understandable. The procedure focused on the lower airways, so your voice may not change much. But we’ll monitor for any swelling or irritation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’ve made it through the night well. Vital signs are stable — pulse 84, BP 132/73, oxygen 100% on trach mask."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Morning. I feel ready to go home. Pain is minimal now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you today. You’ll go home with six oxycodone tablets for breakthrough pain — take one every six hours as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Only six? What if the pain comes back?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The pain should improve over the next few days. If it doesn’t, or if you need more meds, call your pulmonologist. This is just a short course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You have an appointment with interventional pulmonology in four weeks. Your rheumatology follow-up was rescheduled for next week — they’ll manage your polychondritis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I’ll make sure to keep both."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Continue all your regular meds: prednisone, losartan, Esbriet, tobramycin, and famotidine. And remember — triple your steroid dose if you get sick."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And use the injection if I can’t take the pill. I’ll get the MedicAlert bracelet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. Call your pulmonologist immediately if you develop shortness of breath, wheezing, or trouble with your trach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for all the help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2138-04-20 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. You did well. We’ll have the discharge papers ready soon, and you should be home within a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2138-04-20 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check before discharge. You’re alert, breathing comfortably, and your exam is stable. We’re clearing you to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2138-04-20 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. I’m ready."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2138-04-20 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Here’s your discharge summary. It explains why you were here, what was done, and what to do next."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2138-04-20 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I’ll read it carefully."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2138-04-20 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — stay hydrated, rest, and don’t push yourself. Healing takes time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2138-04-20 10:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll take it easy. Appreciate everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2138-04-20 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. ___. We’re here if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2138-04-19 11:30:00",
    "admission_end": "2138-04-20 15:52:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "Mr. ___ was admitted for post-procedural monitoring and pain management following a flexible bronchoscopy with balloon dilation of airway stenoses due to relapsing polychondritis and ___ syndrome. The procedure successfully dilated the left main stem bronchus to 9mm and the bronchus intermedius to 4mm, with no complications. He remained hemodynamically stable, with oxygen saturations at 98–100% on 40% trach mask. Post-procedural pain was managed with oxycodone and acetaminophen. He was educated on adrenal insufficiency risks due to chronic prednisone use, including the need to triple his dose during illness and the use of a Solu-Cortef injection in emergencies. He was discharged home with a short course of oxycodone, instructions to continue all home medications, and follow-up appointments scheduled with interventional pulmonology and rheumatology.",
    "problems": [
      "Relapsing polychondritis",
      "Other specified congenital malformation syndromes, not elsewhere classified",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Other diseases of bronchus, not elsewhere classified",
      "Bronchitis, not specified as acute or chronic",
      "Chronic pseudomonas colonization",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Long term (current) use of systemic steroids",
      "Long term (current) use of antibiotics"
    ]
  }
}
